              ],
              "content": "Fig. 5.3: A 15-cm scale"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_0.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.225,
            0.511,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": "of 1 cm length are further divided into 10 equal parts. The length of one of these smaller parts is called a **millimetre** (**mm**). 1 mm is the smallest value of length that you can measure using this scale. 1 mm is equal to one-tenth of a centimeter (1 mm = 0.1 cm)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.39,
            0.494,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "For measuring larger lengths, we use a larger unit called a **kilometre** (**km**) which is equal to 1000 metres. And for measuring smaller lengths, we use units such as centimetre or millimetre."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.549,
            0.279,
            0.864,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": "**Would it be convenient to use the unit metre to measure larger lengths, such as the length of a railway track between two cities, or to measure smaller lengths, such as the thickness of a page of a book?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.542,
            0.305,
            0.565
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "1 km = 1000 m"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.355,
            0.542,
            0.505,
            0.565
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "1 m = 100 cm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.557,
            0.543,
            0.716,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": "**1 cm = 10 mm**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.619,
            0.757,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": "In some scales, you might have noticed another scale marking. This scale marking is in inches, where 1 inch = 2.54 cm. In earlier days, units, such as inch and foot, were used to measure length. These units are still used by some people."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.746,
            0.771,
            0.818,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.735,
            0.828,
            0.828,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": "**Do you know?**"
        },
        {
